Practice at scanme.nmap.org | LEGAL

nmap 192.168.1.1           | Basic scan(top 1000 ports)
nmap -p 80,443 192.168.1.1 | Scan specific ports
nmap -p- 192.168.1.1       | Scan all 65535 ports
nmap -sV 192.168.1.1       | Detect service versions
nmap -O 192.168.1.1        | OS detection(requires root)
nmap -A 192.168.1.1        | Aggressive scan(OS + version + scripts + traceroute)
nmap -sn 192.168.1.1       | Ping sweep(host discovery only)
nmap -sU 192.168.1.1       | UDP scan

-sS | SYN scan (stealth, default with root)
-sT | TCP connect scan (default without root)
-sU | UDP scan
-sA | ACK scan (firewall mapping)
-sN | Null scan
-sF | FIN scan
-sX | Xmas scan

-T0 | Paranoid (slowest, IDS evasion)
-T1 | Sneaky
-T2 | Polite
-T3 | Normal (default)
-T4 | Aggressive (faster, recommended for LANs)
-T5 | Insane (fastest, may miss results)

nmap -oN output.txt   | Normal text
nmap -oX output.xml   | XML
nmap -oG output.gnmap | Grepable
nmap -oA output       | All three at once

NSE(Nmap Scripting Engine) --script:

auth      | Authentication checks
brute     | Brute-force attacks
discovery | Host/service discovery
exploit   | Exploitation
safe      | Non-intrusive scripts
vuln      | Vulnerability detection

--reason | To see why a port is marked open/closed
